{"id":"2001689461378012509","kind":"article","title":"Execute Program 的课程假设你对先前材料有扎实的回忆","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zH26uarYCm9y6tqzuxaGUzt"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"助记媒介 & 思想工具","date":"2026-02-02","updated":"2026-02-02","votes":3,"comment_count":0,"minutes":1,"chars":654,"keywords":["课程设计","前置知识","检索练习","间隔重复","在线学习"],"summary":"Andy Matuschak 介绍 Execute Program 的课程设计：课程短而聚焦，默认读者能回忆前置知识；平台要求先复习前置课程再解锁新课，以减少重复内容和新课卡顿。作者询问 Gary Bernhardt 后得知，这种设计既符合其写作偏好，也由解锁机制强化。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2001689461378012509","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"lZyzvvDX\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zSsjk5UvNPGrYp8B6DEFCMS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program</a> 的课程很少用来提醒先前材料：它们短小而聚焦。每一课都是在这样的假设下写成的：读者已经学过并且<b>记住了</b>所有前置知识。而这个假设也会被阅读环境所强化：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zHLWyC5LVXZLWE9RmoC1gua\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">在你成功复习其前置课程之前，Execute Program 的课程不会解锁</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"eeukTVUa\">我向 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Gary_Bernhardt\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Gary Bernhardt</a> 询问了这一假设会如何具体地影响他的写作。答案有点不清晰：Gary 原本就更偏好用这种风格来写——Execute Program 只是把它系统化了。</p><p data-pid=\"NV0y8dOi\">根据其界面上的说明：「这个<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zH26uarYCm9y6tqzuxaGUzt\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">假设</a>让我们可以写出更短的课程，并且更少重复你已经学过的想法。它也会让你更不容易在新课程里卡住。」 </p><figure data-size=\"normal\"><img class=\"origin_image zh-lightbox-thumb\" data-original-token=\"v2-cd09a2c3bf6beabe3c455362d0d8c2ab\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-cd09a2c3bf6beabe3c455362d0d8c2ab_r.jpg\" width=\"861\"/></figure><hr/><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><p data-pid=\"oysvl3qF\">Q. Execute Program 的课程如何强化「学生能回忆起所有先前材料」这一假设？ </p><p data-pid=\"qnx2mxFy\">A. <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Execute_Program’s_lessons_don’t_unlock_until_you’ve_successfully_reviewed_their_prerequisites\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">在你成功复习其前置课程之前，Execute Program 的课程不会解锁</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"9xu8JrvJ\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"2001372387644563990\" href=\"#/post/2001372387644563990\">在你成功复习其前置课程之前，Execute Program 的课程不会解锁</a></li><li data-pid=\"D9Jtotwo\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"576613520\" href=\"#/post/576613520\">助记文本可以在一段时间内分小段连载，根据读者的记忆情况排期</a></li><li data-pid=\"AA6su6RZ\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"2000982862988603503\" href=\"#/post/2000982862988603503\">Execute Program 的课程相当短</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"a1kSLiu9\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"LmxKl2KQ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者 gpt-5.2-high，校对 Jarrett Ye<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zH26uarYCm9y6tqzuxaGUzt\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program’s lessons assume solid recall of prior material</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 在你成功复习其前置课程之前，Execute Program 的课程不会解锁 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"2001372387644563990\" href=\"#/post/2001372387644563990\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"2001372387644563990","title":"在你成功复习其前置课程之前，Execute Program 的课程不会解锁","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":9,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"2002091941106586794","title":"在 Execute Program 的复习中，错过的答案不会惩罚学生，除非他们「放弃」","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":5,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"2000982862988603503","title":"Execute Program 的课程相当短","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":2,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"576613520","title":"助记文本可以在一段时间内分小段连载，根据读者的记忆情况排期","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":5,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"2003900630289379481","title":"Execute Program","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":11,"minutes":2,"reason":"延伸引用本文"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[]}